{"name":"Red Dead Redemption","hex":"#bb012d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"dead","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["No longer living; deceased.","Devoid of living things; barren."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Exactly.","Very, absolutely, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead"},{"term":"redemption","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of redeeming or something redeemed.","The recovery, for a fee, of a pawned article."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/redemption"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Dead Redemption","blocks":[{"text":"Red Dead Redemption is a 2010 action-adventure game developed by Rockstar San Diego and published by Rockstar Games. A successor to 2004's Red Dead Revolver, it is the second game in the Red Dead series. Red Dead Redemption is set during the decline of the American frontier in the year 1911. It follows John Marston, a former outlaw who, after his wife and son are taken hostage by the government in ransom for his services as a hired gun, sets out to bring three members of his former gang to justice. The narrative explores themes of the cycle of violence, masculinity, redemption, and the American Dream."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Dead_Redemption"},{"title":"Red Dead","blocks":[{"text":"Red Dead is a series of Western-themed action-adventure games published by Rockstar Games. The first entry in the series, Red Dead Revolver, was released on the PlayStation 2 and Xbox in May 2004. Originally developed by Capcom, Red Dead Revolver borrowed elements from their 1985 arcade title Gun.Smoke, to which it was intended to be a spiritual successor, but the game was cancelled in 2002. Rockstar subsequently acquired the rights to Red Dead Revolver and expanded on it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/21/Official_Red_Dead_logo.png/330px-Official_Red_Dead_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Dead"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg/250px-Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg/250px-Red_Dead_Redemption.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Dead_Redemption.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/RedDeadRedemptionGameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/RedDeadRedemptionGameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Red Dead Redemption features a cover system that lets the player hide behind objects and reach out to fire on people and animals.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedDeadRedemptionGameplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/Red_Dead_Redemption_-_Jack_Marston_as_an_outlaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/Red_Dead_Redemption_-_Jack_Marston_as_an_outlaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Jack Marston's adoption of his father's outlaw status in the game's ending has been viewed as commentary on the theme of redemption: as a manifestation of it;[19] the tragic irony of it;[20] or of its absence and impossibility, and instead the inevitability to repeat the cycle of violence.[21]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Dead_Redemption_-_Jack_Marston_as_an_outlaw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Red_Dead_Redemption_wins_Game_of_the_Year_-_GDCA_2011_07.jpg/500px-Red_Dead_Redemption_wins_Game_of_the_Year_-_GDCA_2011_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Red_Dead_Redemption_wins_Game_of_the_Year_-_GDCA_2011_07.jpg/1280px-Red_Dead_Redemption_wins_Game_of_the_Year_-_GDCA_2011_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig